	-- Intro / how it works ---------------------------------------------------
	RITUAL_TIP_INTRO_TIERS = "• Pick your tier at the Curious Obelisk; clear each tier to unlock the next.|n• The obelisk names what each tier asks for: Tier 3 needs 1 challenge active, Tier 4 needs 2, Tier 5 needs 4, Tier 6 needs 6.|n• Higher tiers give more Spoils and renown. Item level the game recommends, read off the obelisk itself on 20 August: |cffffffffT1 215 · T2 231 · T3 244 · T4 259 · T5 268 · T6 275|r. Hover a tier in the dropdown to check it yourself — these move between seasons. Higher tiers give more Spoils and renown.",
	RITUAL_TIP_INTRO_SCORING = "• Spoils are your score; the Ritual Chest at the end scales with them.|n• Deaths: the first 2 are free, then every death cuts Spoils by 5%, up to a maximum of -50%.|n• Clean clears beat fast pulls — dying costs rewards directly.",
	RITUAL_TIP_INTRO_WEEKLY = "• Each week the tier needed to UNLOCK a challenge drops by one, so everyone unlocks them over time.|n• You cannot unlock all 8 challenges in a single week.|n• Counts for the World row of the Great Vault.|n• Renown boosters: Ritual Tablet (first site of the week), Ritual Tablet Fragment (second site), and Ritual Site Reports (scaled by your Spoils).",
	RITUAL_TIP_INTRO_ORBS = "• In combat, Regeneration Orbs manifest and heal 15% of your health (Renown 1).|n• Orb Potency (Renown 4) increases that healing.|n• Lean on the orbs instead of burning cooldowns on self-healing.",

	-- Daggerspine Point (Eversong Woods) -------------------------------------
	RITUAL_TIP_DAGGERSPINE_OVERVIEW = "• Eversong Woods — Daggerspine Point, on the west coast near Goldenmist Village.|n• Enemies: naga.|n• Active one week at a time; the obelisk shows a purple icon on the map.|n• Enter at the Curious Obelisk and pick your tier + challenges there.",
	RITUAL_TIP_DAGGERSPINE_PHASES = "• A short instanced scenario: clear objectives and enemy waves, then a final boss, then loot the Ritual Chest.|n• Scenario seen at the obelisk: \"A Strike From the Sea\" — the naga leader Selen'vjar (final-boss kill still to confirm).|n• A site may run more than one scenario layout — to confirm in-game.",
	RITUAL_TIP_DAGGERSPINE_NOTES = "• Tainted Bone Pile (unlocks the Tainted Corpses challenge): /way 66.09 62.58.|n• Dark Obelisks (Malevolent Boons quest — investigate any 5; 9 spawns): 66.6/38.8 · 64.7/49.8 · 63.8/70.9 · 39.2/76.2 · 35.3/63.2 · 50/42 · 42/56 · 62/62 · 44.8/47.3.|n• Small treasures and Regeneration Orbs are scattered around the site.",

	-- Broken Throne (Zul'Aman) -----------------------------------------------
	RITUAL_TIP_BROKENTHRONE_OVERVIEW = "• Zul'Aman — Broken Throne, in the south of the zone.|n• Enemies: Twilight's Blade cultists.|n• Active one week at a time; the obelisk shows a purple icon on the map.|n• Enter at the Curious Obelisk and pick your tier + challenges there.",
	RITUAL_TIP_BROKENTHRONE_PHASES = "• A short instanced scenario: clear objectives and enemy waves, then a final boss, then loot the Ritual Chest.|n• Scenario seen at the obelisk: \"A Corrupted Path\" — Faithbreaker Ger'lok corrupts everything with the Void and is the final boss.|n• DEADLY on the later bosses (e.g. the Corrupted Amani Dragonhawk): void mirrors (Dissonant Reflections) keep spawning and cast Dissonant Realities — a massive burst on everything within 100 yards. You can't outrange it: INTERRUPT the cast and the mirror vanishes instantly. Save your kick for exactly this.|n• Corrupted Amani Dragonhawk: a Binding Nebula traps you — you CANNOT leave until you KILL the nebula itself, so burst it down the moment you're caught. Trapped players die to Volatile Plumage (the feather eruption hits for hundreds of thousands); never stand in front of the Shadowflame Breath.|n• A site may run more than one scenario layout — to confirm in-game.",
	RITUAL_TIP_BROKENTHRONE_NOTES = "• Tainted Bone Pile (unlocks the Tainted Corpses challenge): /way 47.91 36.52.|n• Dark Obelisks (Malevolent Boons quest — investigate any 5; 6 spawns): 61/50 · 41/50 · 45/59 · 42/68 · 55/58 · 54/54.|n• Destroying the Dark Obelisks strips the buffs that empower the site's enemies — clearing them makes the bosses noticeably easier (only leave them up if you're going for the no-obelisk achievement).|n• Small treasures and Regeneration Orbs are scattered around the site.",
	-- Ritual Boss Coach (boss-venster; EditBox → {SPELL:} mag hier wél).
	RITUAL_BOSS_DRAGONHAWK_STEPS = "• {SPELL:1291610} drops little RED POOLS. Stand in one to soak it: you take only a small hit. A pool nobody stands in erupts for huge Shadowflame damage and can kill the whole group. One player per pool is enough.|n• {SPELL:1284125}: a nebula forms under a random player. It hurts every second and slows you by 40%. You cannot walk out while it lives, so kill the nebula to get free.|n• {SPELL:1284081}: void mirrors keep appearing in the middle and cast Dissonant Realities, a huge hit on everyone within 100 yards. You cannot outrun it. Interrupt the cast and the mirror vanishes. Save your kick for this.|n• Stand BEHIND the dragonhawk. Its frontal Shadowflame Breath is deadly.",
	RITUAL_BOSS_DRAGONHAWK_QUICK = "Red pools: Stand in a red pool so it cannot blow up on everyone.|nMirror: Kick the spell of the mirror in the middle, or it hits everyone hard.|nNebula: If a dark cloud traps you, kill the cloud to get out.",
	RITUAL_BOSS_GERLOK_STEPS = "• He summons minions that make him take (almost) no damage. Burn every add the instant it spawns. The adds charge with a fire channel that nearly one-shots, so step out of it.|n• {SPELL:1273031} is THE cast to interrupt: a big hit on everyone nearby. Not every cast is kickable, so save your interrupt for it.|n• {SPELL:1279186} is spammed. Break line of sight behind the pillars.|n• Keep him ON his platform. Pulling him down or off it resets the fight (Rob, live). The space is cramped, but don't chase room below.|n• Embers challenge: Embers left burning make him much stronger. One player on Wowhead saw about 60% more health and damage with all four up. Kill the marked mobs around each Ember before the boss to put it out.",
	RITUAL_BOSS_GERLOK_QUICK = "Adds: Kill his helpers at once, because while they live he takes almost no damage.|nKick: Save your interrupt for Shadowbolt Volley, his big hit on everyone.|nPillars: Hide behind a pillar so his Shadow Blast cannot hit you.",
	RAID_BOSS_ROTMIRE_STEPS = "• One boss and one loop that repeats until he dies. Bloodlust on the pull. Every {SPELL:1221787} adds a Rotting Pustules stack that stays, so raid damage keeps rising: the longer the fight, the harder.|n• {SPELL:1221622}: circles on the floor show where adds appear. Step out of them, or you are knocked away and hurt badly. Each add (Shroomling) chases one player: walk it into one tight pile near the boss, so the raid kills them all together.|n• Kill every add before his energy bar is full. At 100 energy he casts {SPELL:1221637}: a hit on everyone, a knockback and a 16-second DoT. An add still alive then gets Fungal Frenzy: full health, and it can no longer be stunned or interrupted.|n• After {SPELL:1221637} every add corpse grows into a Bursting Shroom. Kill them all within about 16 seconds: each one left explodes on the whole raid, and more than one explosion usually wipes you. That is why the adds die in one pile.|n• {SPELL:1222088} slows a few players and hurts them. Walk to the edge of the room before it ends: it leaves a patch ({SPELL:1222129}) that stays. Keep the middle and the add pile clear, and step out of any patch.|n• On Heroic and Mythic: a Sporecap add appears as well and does not move. Interrupt its Poison Burst every single time, or the whole raid stacks a DoT. Bring the other adds to it and kill them there.|n• On Mythic: Funglings come too. A Shroomling corpse within 10 yards of a Fungling corpse makes a Bursting Doom Shroom, and that wipes the raid. Kill the two kinds in two separate spots.",
	RAID_BOSS_ROTMIRE_QUICK_DPS = "Kill every add in the pile before his bar is full, then kill the shrooms at once.",
	RAID_BOSS_ROTMIRE_QUICK_HEALER = "Damage gets bigger every loop, so plan cooldowns for the big hit when his bar is full.",
	RAID_BOSS_ROTMIRE_QUICK_TANK = "Swap with the other tank after every big punch, and keep the boss next to the add pile.",
	RAID_BOSS_ROTMIRE_QUICK = "Adds: Pull the small mushroom adds into one pile and kill them before his energy bar is full.|nShrooms: When his bar is full, dead adds grow into shrooms, so kill those fast before they explode.|nVines: If vines slow you, walk to the edge of the room so their leftover patch stays out of the way.",
	RAID_BOSS_ROTMIRE_TANK = "• Swap with the other tank after every {SPELL:1221781}: it throws you up and makes you take more physical damage for 14 seconds (35% on Normal, 75% on Heroic and Mythic). Use a defensive for the hit.|n• Keep the boss next to the add pile, so the raid hits him while they kill the adds. On Heroic and Mythic: bring him to the Sporecap.",
	RAID_BOSS_ROTMIRE_HEALER = "• Raid damage climbs all fight: every {SPELL:1221787} adds a Rotting Pustules stack, so each loop is harder than the last.|n• Plan raid cooldowns for {SPELL:1221637} (a hit plus a 16-second DoT on everyone) and for any Bursting Shroom that explodes.|n• The tank hit by {SPELL:1221781} takes much more physical damage for 14 seconds.",
	RAID_BOSS_ROTMIRE_DPS = "• Cleave the adds in their pile, and have every one dead before {SPELL:1221637}. Then switch to the Bursting Shrooms at once.|n• On Heroic and Mythic: interrupt the Sporecap's Poison Burst every time.|n• On Mythic: Shroomlings and Funglings die in two separate spots, at least 10 yards apart.",
	RAID_BOSS_NYMRISSA_STEPS = "• |cffffd100The way in is UNDERWATER|r — a submerged cave, so your breath bar runs before the fight does. Air bubbles around the entrance top it up.|n• One boss, one loop that repeats until she dies. It counts for the Raid row of your Great Vault.|n• |cffffd100The murlocs are the fight.|r {SPELL:1257717} puts a big bubble in the middle and murlocs run for it. Kill or slow them BEFORE they reach it — every one that gets in becomes a Berserker that hits the whole group every 3 seconds. Bring the boss to the biggest pack; ranged take the stragglers.|n• Whirlpools circle the room with one gap between them — stack in the gap.|n• When a whirlpool reaches the bubble it pops: damage on everyone plus a knockback. Stand so you are not thrown into the water — there are sharks.|n• {SPELL:1313393}: if it hits you, you leave frost orbs where you walk. Drop them together, away from the bubble and the paths. On Normal don't touch them (stacking damage and slippery ice); on Heroic and Mythic they must be picked up, or they shatter on the whole group.|n• {SPELL:1260837} is four seconds of damage on everyone — a healing cooldown. On Heroic and Mythic each one makes her hit harder: the slow soft enrage.|n• After 10 minutes comes the hard enrage: the pull is over.|n• Bloodlust on the pull.|n• From the live guides and DBM's current mod, not yet run by us — tell us what you saw.",
	RAID_BOSS_NYMRISSA_TANK = "• Normal and Heroic: {SPELL:1282937} is several seconds of heavy hits on you — use a defensive. Nothing to aim.|n• Mythic: {SPELL:1268562} is a line that pushes you back and stacks; point it away from the group (through the icy patches, it washes them away) and swap with the other tank on the stacks.|n• Keep her near the biggest murloc pack, never on top of the bubble.",
	RAID_BOSS_NYMRISSA_HEALER = "• Plan cooldowns for {SPELL:1260837} (four seconds on everyone) and for the bubble popping. Both are predictable.|n• A murloc Berserker pulses the whole group every 3 seconds until it dies — a missed murloc is where healing falls apart.",
	RAID_BOSS_NYMRISSA_DPS = "• Murlocs first, always: kill or slow them before they reach the bubble; stuns, roots and knockbacks work. A Berserker dies immediately.|n• Mythic: kill the Frostscale first — it makes the murlocs around it take 99% less damage.|n• Then back on the boss.",
	RITUAL_BOSS_MINDBREAKER_STEPS = "• Void-Infused Mindbreaker: the Empowered Mindbreaker of Daggerspine Point stage 2, Beast From the Deep. A deep creature Lady Selen'vjar supercharges with stolen void magic.|n• One player's report on Wowhead: the ray it shoots at you is deadly. Keep running over the healing orbs, and always know where the next one is.|n• That is all we have. No source lists its abilities yet. Until then the general rule: interrupt what you can and step out of ground effects.|n• If you fight it, tell us on Discord what it did and it goes in.",
	RITUAL_BOSS_SELENVJAR_STEPS = "• Lady Selen'vjar: naga leader and end boss of Daggerspine Point (Eversong Woods, /way 34.9 65.4).|n• Stages: 1) Ritual Roles: her captains guard the ritual and drain void essence. 2) Beast From the Deep: she empowers a Mindbreaker. 3) Summoner's Fall: she fights you herself.|n• No source describes her abilities yet: not Wowhead, not a guide, not a forum post. Players on Wowhead do call her much easier than Faithbreaker Ger'lok.|n• If you fight her, tell us on Discord what she did and it goes in.",
	RITUAL_ALERT_BINDING_NEBULA = "Binding Nebula! -> kill the nebula",
	RITUAL_ALERT_SHADOWBOLT = "Interrupt Shadowbolt Volley!",
	RITUAL_ALERT_DISSONANT = "Interrupt Dissonant Reflections!",

	-- Challenges -------------------------------------------------------------
	RITUAL_TIP_TENDRILS_MECHANIC = "• Grasping tendrils spawn with a swirling green circle — step out or you get rooted and take damage.|n• Raises Spoils while active.",
	RITUAL_TIP_TENDRILS_UNLOCK = "• Loot a Ritual Chest at the end of any site, then turn in the quest \"Ritual Site Challenge Report: Tendrils\".",
	RITUAL_TIP_MANIFESTATIONS_MECHANIC = "• Spirits manifest and cast spells — interrupt them or take withering magic.|n• Raises Spoils while active.",
	RITUAL_TIP_MANIFESTATIONS_UNLOCK = "• Clear a Tier 3 site, then speak with Ranger Captain Lilatha in Silvermoon (the required tier drops each week).",
	RITUAL_TIP_ALARMBELLS_MECHANIC = "• Killing enemies summons reinforcements; the bigger and stronger the pull you kill, the stronger the adds.|n• Raises Spoils while active.",
	RITUAL_TIP_ALARMBELLS_UNLOCK = "• Clear a Tier 4 site, then speak with Lady Darkglen in Silvermoon (the required tier drops each week).",
	RITUAL_TIP_MALEVOLENTBOONS_MECHANIC = "• Dark obelisks buff nearby enemies — destroy the obelisks to strip the buffs.|n• Raises Spoils while active.",
	RITUAL_TIP_MALEVOLENTBOONS_UNLOCK = "• Clear a Tier 2 site for a quest from Lady Darkglen, then investigate 5 Dark Obelisks inside a site (the required tier drops each week).",
	RITUAL_TIP_TAINTEDCORPSES_MECHANIC = "• Slain enemies leave a pool of deadly void magic — move out of it.|n• Raises Spoils while active.",
	RITUAL_TIP_TAINTEDCORPSES_UNLOCK = "• Loot a Tainted Bone Pile inside a Tier 2+ site (see the site notes for its location), then turn in the quest.",
	RITUAL_TIP_REINFORCED_MECHANIC = "• Extra enemies are spread throughout the site — expect denser packs.|n• Raises Spoils while active (one of the larger boosts).",
	RITUAL_TIP_REINFORCED_UNLOCK = "• Clear a Tier 2 site, then speak with Ranger Captain Lilatha in Silvermoon (the required tier drops each week).",
	RITUAL_TIP_PATROLS_MECHANIC = "• Elite enemies patrol the site — avoid their paths where you can.|n• Raises Spoils while active.",
	RITUAL_TIP_PATROLS_UNLOCK = "• \"Procure\" unique treasures from a Tier 3+ site (the required tier drops each week).",
	RITUAL_TIP_EMBERS_MECHANIC = "• Random enemies AND the final boss are empowered, marked by a floating orb above them.|n• Raises Spoils while active (one of the larger boosts).",
	RITUAL_TIP_EMBERS_UNLOCK = "• Loot an Ember of Power inside a Tier 4 site to start the quest (the required tier drops each week).",
})

